    "total_non_empty_paragraphs": 16,
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "paragraph_index": 0,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "PRACTICAL-4",
        "char_count": 11
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 3,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "AIM : Perform forensic image acquisition of the evidence drive provided using Guymager. Tool used : Guymager",
        "char_count": 108
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 4,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Guymager is a GUI-based imaging tool available in most Linux forensic distributions such as Kali Linux. Guymager is not a Windows program. It runs only on Linux. It can acquire bit-by-bit images of storage devices and automatically calculates integrity hashes.",
        "char_count": 260
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 5,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Steps",
        "char_count": 5
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 6,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Open Terminal in ubuntu",
        "char_count": 23
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 8,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Launch Guymager as root sudo guymager",
        "char_count": 37
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 12,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Guymager lists all connected storage devices. Identify the evidence drive (e.g., /dev/sdb).",
        "char_count": 91
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 15,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Right-click on the device you need to image. Choose “Acquire Image.” This will bring up the Acquire Image screen.",
        "char_count": 113
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 18,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "This will bring up the Acquire Image screen. Add the details for the image. Select the Image Directory choose or create a folder to store the image.",
        "char_count": 148
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 20,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Click Start to begin the imaging process.",
        "char_count": 41
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 22,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "When imaging is complete the acquisition screen will show Finished.",
        "char_count": 67
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 24,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Now, you can simply close the Guymager screen and open the directory where you told",
        "char_count": 83
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 25,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Guymager to store the image. Here, you'll see two files: the image file (with the suffix .E01 for our file, since we chose Expert Witness Format) and the metadata file (with the suffix",
        "char_count": 184
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 26,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": ".info).",
        "char_count": 7
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 29,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "output_heading",
        "text": "OUTPUT",
        "char_count": 6
      },
      {
        "paragraph_index": 30,
        "style": "Normal",
        "category": "body",
        "text": "Successfully acquired a forensic image of the given evidence drive using Guymager and verified its integrity using generated hash values.",
        "char_count": 137
      }
    ]
  },
